{{also|Tinker}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tɪŋkə(ɹ)/}}, {{SAMPA|/tINk@(r)/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪŋkə(r)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|tinkere|lang=enm}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# an [[itinerant]] tinsmith and [[mender]] of [[household]] [[utensil]]s made of tin
# {{dated|chiefly|British|and|Irish|offensive}} A member of the [[travelling]] community. A [[gypsy]].
# {{context|usually with "little"}} A [[mischievous]] person, especially a playful, [[impish]] youngster.
# Someone who repairs, or attempts repair on anything mechanical (tinkers) or invents.
# The act of repair or invention.

====Synonyms====
